{"id": "EUVD-2026-48935", "enisaUuid": "f13b3159-4849-3466-bc34-b30be9ab4a71", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: use opener credentials for ADS I/O\n\nAlternate data streams are stored as xattrs. Unlike regular file I/O,\ntheir read and write paths therefore call VFS xattr helpers which recheck\ninode permissions and LSM policy using the current task credentials.\n\nRun ADS I/O with the credentials captured when the SMB handle was opened.", "datePublished": "2026-07-25T08:50:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:43:21", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2ad5509dd576ae16d252d4698daf03002f9e0234", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a8f5d39971bbad9340d49cd41b0e2da9452a649d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2b4592cea214683de0f2ce6f8c22c097fb0ea1ab", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/52a56cf53ec834c44ac1b4d16d585f26613ee5ce", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/baa5e094886fffa7e6272edcb5e08be5ce28262c"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-64391", "GHSA-83mf-wfc5-x4x3"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.46, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02f18b47-3fe3-3f81-81dc-546a4d2bc28a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "2b6dbe69-5688-3153-a2b4-2d58f0a321c1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f44158485826c076335d6860d35872271a83791d <2ad5509dd576ae16d252d4698daf03002f9e0234"}, {"id": "58aafe39-99d7-398d-a6b5-5ad37e8f7f0f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.4"}, {"id": "5f84a013-013d-3df9-a4e2-c301382e3deb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f44158485826c076335d6860d35872271a83791d <2b4592cea214683de0f2ce6f8c22c097fb0ea1ab"}, {"id": "71c30c4a-255f-3966-9c59-4775fe0b22c7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"nam